      "id": "https://www.archdaily.com/1186540/wiki-world-forest-store-wiki-world",
      "url": "https://www.archdaily.com/1186540/wiki-world-forest-store-wiki-world",
      "title": "[ArchDaily] Wiki World Forest Store / Wiki World",
      "content_html": "<img src=\"https://images.adsttc.com/media/images/6ac7/14df/07c3/d100/017f/e141/large_jpg/02.jpg?1791431947\" style=\"width:100%;max-height:300px;object-fit:cover;\"/>\n<p>The birth of the Wiki World Forest Store stems from the ongoing natural architecture practice carried out by Wiki World. Although we have always insisted on building with the zeroprint concept and 100% timber structures, along with the birth of one wilderness home after another, there is always wood that inevitably becomes waste. Who wants to be abandoned leftover scraps? So we wondered: could waste materials be used to build a house? Could leftover scraps also have unrealistic fantasies and be turned into interesting wooden products? Therefore, we planned this building and the products inside it. The Wiki World Forest Store is located at the entrance of Merryda Wiki World-Secret Camp, at the edge of a forest. Pure wood and glass are connected, and the recyclable concept does not require more complex craftsmanship.</p>",
      "date_published": "2026-10-10T02:00:00+00:00",
      "authors": [
        {
          "name": "ArchDaily",
          "url": "https://www.archdaily.com"
        }
      ],
