      "title": "[Dezeen] Home in Kyoto is a \"subtle rearranging\" of familiar spaces",
      "content_html": "<img src=\"http://static.dezeen.com/uploads/2026/10/sugi-house-ujizono-architects-kyoto_dezeen_2364_sq_0-411x411.jpg\" style=\"width:100%;max-height:300px;object-fit:cover;\"/>\n<p>An expansive gabled ceiling illuminated by clerestory windows shelters the open living spaces of Sugi House, a home in Kyoto designed by Japanese studio Ujizono Architects. Ujizono Architects co-founders Kazuki Ujigawa and Mirai Ozono aimed to \"subtly rearrange\" the form of east Kyoto's typical homes, contrasting an enclosed ground floor with an expansive first floor.</p>\n<p>The post <a href=\"https://www.dezeen.com/2026/10/09/sugi-house-ujizono-architects-kyoto/\">Home in Kyoto is a \"subtle rearranging\" of familiar spaces</a> appeared first on <a href=\"https://www.dezeen.com\">Dezeen</a>.</p>",
